<!--
  ANALOG_GROUND.mp3 — ground VHF stream from rtl-airband-ground.service.
  Added 2026-05-26 as part of the MA/SL split-process architecture
  (docs/rspduo_ma_sl_split.md).  Mirrors the existing /ANALOG.mp3
  block.

  Fallback note (2026-05-27): each analog mount now has its OWN
  keepalive (/keepalive-analog.mp3 for /ANALOG.mp3,
  /keepalive-ground.mp3 for /ANALOG_GROUND.mp3).  Sharing one
  keepalive caused icecast's source_move_clients to migrate the
  ground VLC listener onto /ANALOG.mp3 every time the analog
  publisher re-attached, producing a doubled-audio echo on the
  BT speaker.  See rtl-airband-keepalive-ground.service for the
  matching ffmpeg silence source.

  Cutover step: the script inserts the mount block below into
  icecast.xml right after the ANALOG.mp3 block.  ``systemctl reload
  icecast2`` picks it up without disrupting active listeners on
  other mounts.  Do not put XML tags inside this comment body — the
  cutover script's regex looks for the FIRST mount-block-shaped
  match and a tagged comment can fool it.
-->
<mount>
  <mount-name>/ANALOG_GROUND.mp3</mount-name>
  <type>audio/mpeg</type>
  <fallback-mount>/keepalive-ground.mp3</fallback-mount>
  <fallback-override>1</fallback-override>
</mount>
